Q: Using CSS to set default font A: <p>I think that the important thing is to have the &quot;*&quot; in the rule, so:</p>
<pre><code>* {
    font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, &quot;Courier&quot;, monospace;
}
</code></pre>
<p>would be the best, or maybe</p>
<pre><code>body * {
    font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, &quot;Courier&quot;, monospace;
}
</code></pre>
<p>or</p>
<pre><code>html * {
    font-family: &quot;Courier New&quot;, &quot;Courier&quot;, monospace;
}
</code></pre>
